---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import Hero from '../../components/sections/Hero.astro';
import Card from '../../components/ui/Card.astro';
import Button from '../../components/ui/Button.astro';

const buttondownList = 'queryfarm-dispatch';
---

<PageLayout
  title="Newsletter"
  description="Subscribe to the Query.Farm newsletter for updates on new DuckDB extensions, VGI releases, and posts from the team."
>
  <Hero
    title="Query.Farm Newsletter"
    subtitle="Updates on new DuckDB extensions, VGI releases, and the occasional deep dive — straight to your inbox. No spam, easy unsubscribe."
  />

  <section class="py-16 lg:py-24 bg-white">
    <div class="section-container">
      <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto">
        <Card padding="lg">
          <form
            action={`https://buttondown.com/api/emails/embed-subscribe/${buttondownList}`}
            method="post"
            target="popupwindow"
            onsubmit={`window.open('https://buttondown.com/${buttondownList}', 'popupwindow')`}
            class="space-y-4"
          >
            <label for="bd-email" class="block text-sm font-medium text-soil-800">
              Email address
            </label>
            <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-3">
              <input
                id="bd-email"
                type="email"
                name="email"
                required
                placeholder="you@example.com"
                class="flex-1 px-4 py-3 rounded-lg border border-soil-300 bg-white text-soil-900 placeholder:text-soil-500 focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-harvest-500 focus:border-harvest-500"
              />
              <Button type="submit" variant="primary" size="md">
                Subscribe
              </Button>
            </div>
            <p class="text-xs text-soil-500">
              You'll be redirected to a Buttondown confirmation page. We use Buttondown — your email isn't shared with anyone else.
            </p>
          </form>
        </Card>

        <div class="mt-12">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-soil-900 mb-4">What you'll get</h2>
          <ul class="space-y-3 text-soil-700">
            <li class="flex items-start">
              <svg class="w-5 h-5 mr-2 mt-0.5 text-harvest-600 flex-shrink-0" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" />
              </svg>
              <span>New DuckDB extension releases — what they do, how to install, what to watch out for.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start">
              <svg class="w-5 h-5 mr-2 mt-0.5 text-harvest-600 flex-shrink-0" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" />
              </svg>
              <span>VGI updates — new language SDKs, protocol changes, real-world usage notes.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start">
              <svg class="w-5 h-5 mr-2 mt-0.5 text-harvest-600 flex-shrink-0" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" />
              </svg>
              <span>Occasional deep dives — DuckDB internals, performance, design decisions we made and why.</span>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <p class="mt-12 text-sm text-soil-600 text-center">
          Prefer RSS? <a href="/blog" class="text-harvest-700 underline">Read the blog</a> directly.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</PageLayout>
